 order-B | aborted   |    0 | card declined for 5000.00
 order-C | aborted   |    0 | address not deliverable: nowhere
 order-D | completed |    4 | 
(4 rows)

== timer: start order-E with a 30s fraud hold; the process exits while the saga waits ==

## 6. Durable timer
   concept: a saga that has to wait (here a 30s fraud hold, in real life days) does not keep a process alive; it writes wake_at to the saga log and the process is free to exit
   19:47:30 starting order-E
   [order-E] started {"sku":"keyboard","qty":1,"amount":"42.00","address":"Lille","holdSec":30}
      -> HTTP POST inventory-service/reservations/order-E
   [order-E] step 1 reserveInventory: ok
      -> HTTP POST payments-service/charges/order-E
   [order-E] step 2 chargePayment: ok
   19:47:30 [order-E] step 3 fraudHold: sleep 30s -> saga log says waiting, wake_at 19:48:00; this process stops driving it
   19:47:30 timer process exits; order-E now exists only as a row
   id    |  state  | step |            wake_at            
---------+---------+------+-------------------------------
 order-E | waiting |    3 | 2026-09-27 19:48:00.555308+00
(1 row)

